  "answer_markdown": "The Mistral models that support the FIM (fill-in-the-middle) feature are Codestral (`codestral-2501`) and Codestral (`codestral-2508`). [2] This is confirmed in the model capability matrix, which lists these two models under the FIM column. [2]\n\nAdditionally, the Codestral model card for both versions explicitly mentions FIM as a supported feature. [3][5]\n\nNo other Mistral models are mentioned as supporting the FIM feature in the provided sources.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Model | FIM | \n| --- | --- | \n| [Codestral](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/codestral-25-01) | yes | \n| [Codestral](https://docs.mistral.ai/models/codestral-25-08) | yes | \n- **[FIM](https://docs.mistral.ai/mistral-vibe/using-fim-api)** (`fim`), 2 models: Codestral (`codestral-2501`), Codestral (`codestral-2508`)"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Codestral specializes in low-latency, high-frequency tasks such as fill-in-the-middle (FIM) and code generation."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "Codestral specializes in low-latency, high-frequency tasks such as fill-in-the-middle (FIM), code correction and test generation."
    }
  ],
