message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To use Vibe Code within a specific Workspace, the developer must hold the **`mistral_code_user`** Workspace role. This role grants access to Vibe Code, which includes features such as read/write access to the filesystem, a shell, and configurable tools to read files, run commands, write code, and open pull requests under supervision [9].\n\nFor creating an API key, the key should be created with the **Workspace scope**, specifically for the Workspace where Vibe Code will be used. The API key will then use that Workspace's quota, rate limits, and resources [3].\n\nHere is the code snippet to create an API key programmatically using the Admin API:\n\n```bash\ncurl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/admin/api-keys \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\": \"My Vibe Code Key\", \"workspace_uuid\": \"<workspace_uuid>\", \"user_id\": \"<user_id>\"}'\n```\n\nReplace `<workspace_uuid>` with the UUID of the target Workspace and `<user_id>` with the user's ID [15].\n\nAdditionally, the API key should be scoped to the Workspace where Vibe Code will be used, ensuring that it has access to the appropriate resources and connectors [3].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 9,
      "quote": "Vibe Code is Vibe's coding mode. With read/write access to your filesystem, a shell, and a configurable set of tools, it can read files, run commands, write code, and open pull requests on your behalf, under your supervision."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "API keys are scoped to the Workspace where they were created. Requests made with a key use that Workspace's quota, rate limits, and resources."
    },
    {
      "n": 15,
      "quote": "curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/admin/api-keys \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\": \"My Vibe Code Key\", \"workspace_uuid\": \"<workspace_uuid>\", \"user_id\": \"<user_id>\"}'"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

